`/app/lib/ansible/plugins/shell/powershell.py`
- Accepts bytes as input and returns bytes
- Scans for CLIXML headers (`b"#< CLIXML\r\n"`)
- Detects complete CLIXML blocks (from header to `</Objs>`)
- Decodes CLIXML data as UTF-8, with cp437 fallback if UTF-8 fails
- Parses CLIXML using `_parse_clixml`
- Replaces CLIXML blocks with decoded text
- Preserves surrounding data and trailing bytes on the same line
- Handles parsing errors and incomplete blocks by leaving original data 
unchanged
- Detects CLIXML blocks split across lines and leaves them unchanged

### 3. Updated imports in `/app/lib/ansible/plugins/connection/ssh.py`
- Added `_replace_stderr_clixml` to the import from 
`ansible.plugins.shell.powershell`

### 4. Updated `exec_command` method in 
`/app/lib/ansible/plugins/connection/ssh.py`
- Replaced the conditional logic that only parsed CLIXML when stderr started 
with `b"#< CLIXML"`
- Now calls `_replace_stderr_clixml` for all Windows targets, which handles 
CLIXML blocks anywhere in stderr

